WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.599
The intestine is never merely a digestive tube. Its

00:00:03.599 --> 00:00:06.048
immune interface is continually deciding what to

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:07.798
tolerate and what to confront.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.097
The gastrointestinal wall is an immune interface, with

00:00:20.097 --> 00:00:22.832
specialised barriers and molecular signals operating

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:23.744
beside digestion.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.576
The immune system must distinguish threats from

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:37.255
food-associated and resident signals. Breakdown can

00:00:37.255 --> 00:00:38.595
produce complex pathology.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.135
The chapter examines autoimmune gastrointestinal

00:00:49.135 --> 00:00:52.356
diseases and their aetiology, considering immunological

00:00:52.356 --> 00:00:56.652
mechanisms rather than treating all inflammation as one

00:00:56.652 --> 00:00:57.189
diagnosis.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.154
Histological patterns, molecular mechanisms and

00:01:05.154 --> 00:01:07.859
clinical presentation require careful reconciliation

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:11.645
before attributing symptoms to a particular immune

00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:12.186
disorder.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.349
Pathways discussed in a review vary across diseases. An

00:01:21.349 --> 00:01:24.815
autoimmune mechanism should not be presumed for every

00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:26.547
inflammatory or eosinophilic presentation.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.617
Mechanistic plausibility should be weighed against

00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:38.256
measured evidence and disease-specific diagnostic

00:01:38.256 --> 00:01:38.784
criteria.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.684
Part One assembles mechanistic evidence, keeping the

00:01:49.684 --> 00:01:51.995
boundaries between distinct disorders visible.
